# Everything the image must NOT inherit from a developer's machine.
#
# Without this, `COPY . .` drags the host `node_modules` into the build. In a pnpm workspace that
# is a tree of symlinks into `/repo/node_modules/.pnpm` — paths that do not resolve inside the
# container — and pnpm then decides the store is stale and tries to delete the directory, which it
# refuses to do without a TTY:
#
#     [ERR_PNPM_ABORTED_REMOVE_MODULES_DIR_NO_TTY]
#
# That is the loud failure. The quiet one matters more: a build that copies host `node_modules`
# and happens to work is an image whose contents depend on whoever built it, which is the exact
# thing a lockfile and `--frozen-lockfile` exist to prevent.

# ── Dependencies and build output. The image builds these itself.
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
.next
**/.next
.turbo
**/.turbo
storybook-static
**/storybook-static
*.tsbuildinfo

# ── Local state that must never reach an image.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# ── Version control and CI.
.git
.gitignore
.github
.husky

# ── Editor and OS noise.
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ── Documentation and specification. Large, and no build step reads it.
docs
*.md
!README.md

# ── Test and coverage artefacts.
coverage
**/coverage
playwright-report
test-results

# NOTE: `patches/` is deliberately NOT ignored. `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` applies it, and
# an image built without it silently differs from every other environment (`SB-26`).
